[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-HEADER-GREETING
TITLE: Greeting

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-61
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When a member is logged in with a valid members-only application session, the Header Greeting SHALL display a greeting that includes that member's name.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The greeting shows a logged-in member that the Header recognizes the session and identifies the member by name.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Greeting form is Hello, followed by the member name (GSSC5-22).
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-22
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PHLR-8
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-62
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Greeting SHALL appear first among the Header right-side action controls in place of the Header Login control when a member is logged in, SHALL be omitted when no member is logged in, SHALL open a dropdown on hover that contains the Header Member Access and Header Logout controls, and SHALL be separated from the following right-side text control by a vertical divider.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Greeting replaces Login in the right-side order. Hover reveals Members site access and Logout without crowding the Header bar.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-22
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PHLR-8
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-63
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Greeting SHALL use the sans-serif theme font and the dark-green theme token for its text color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Greeting shares Header action text tokens so it reads with Login, Contact, and related controls.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-22
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PHLR-8
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-HEADER-LOGOUT
TITLE: Logout

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-64
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When a member is logged in, the Header Logout control SHALL end that member's members-only application session and leave the visitor on the public page.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Logout ends the Member Frontend session through the existing backend logout and keeps the visitor on the current public page.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-22
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PHLR-9
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-65
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Header Logout control SHALL appear in the Header Greeting dropdown when a member is logged in, and SHALL be omitted when no member is logged in.
